<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FlexiPage xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>decorate</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End Customer must be Unified to update quote line to Won!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When a quote is submitted using Write In End Customer, the end customer must be validated through the unification process by the UCD team. The UCD team may require additional information about the end customer, like a physical address or URL, to complete the unification process. The team will email the AE, if available on the quote, or the SDM directly requesting additional information about the end customer. If you receive an email from central.customer.data.operations@intel.com asking for clarification about an end customer, it is imperative you respond as quickly as possible. If the UCD team does not get a response within 30 days, they will stop the unification process, which will prevent the quote line from being marked as Won and will delay any rebate payment on the request. If you need to retrigger the unification process, please email My.Deals.Support@intel.com.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WW30 Release&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After the WW30 release, AEs will have visibility into the Approved ECAP Price of quotes they are named on. Visibility to this price should be kept confidential and should not be shared with others. It also should not be used to phish for pricing discounts. AEs should however use this price within the appropriate Opportunity to ensure the most accurate information is reflected in Sales CRM.”&lt;/p&gt;</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>flexipage:richText</componentName>
                <identifier>flexipage_richText</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
